{"entryId":"1818","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1818:1","sourceSha256":"ae728528c60f90aae03ae839ad5dc5cdf53b46b51132e5f9cb2ec81c1f997d6d","englishSha256":"bdd311f6cffe808f41346e9f7d500a852251bda57c96d5f5d0312349465c9f64","citations":[{"id":"1818:1:link-01","he":[19,35],"en":[69,109],"target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","assessment":"Yuchasin gives Levite and gatekeeper. The Bavli distinguishes his assigned gatekeeping from Yehoshua’s singing.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Arakhin 11b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Arakhin_11b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-02","he":[69,113],"en":[128,147],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_56b.1"},"reference":"Sukkah 56b:1","assessment":"The Bavli explains the two extra loaves for the incoming priestly watch as compensation for shutting the doors.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sukkah 56b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_56b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sukkah 56a:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_56a.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sukkah 56b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_56b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-03","he":[147,190],"en":[343,348],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Tamid_1.1"},"reference":"Mishnah Tamid 1:1","assessment":"Tamid names three priestly guard stations and gives the courtyard keys to priestly elders. Middot separately names Levite guards at the gates. Keep Yuchasin’s inference attributed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Tamid 1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Tamid_1.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Middot 1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Middot_1.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-04","he":[191,367],"en":[353,381],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosefta_Shekalim_%28Lieberman%29_2.14"},"reference":"Tosefta Shekalim (Lieberman) 2:14","assessment":"Both Tosefta witnesses carry this roster with spelling variants. Mishnah Shekalim has Ben Gever for closing the gates and accords Ben Arzah a different duty.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosefta Shekalim (Lieberman) 2:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosefta_Shekalim_%28Lieberman%29_2.14"},"witness":"The Tosefta according to to codex Vienna. Third Augmented Edition, JTS 2001"},{"reference":"Tosefta Shekalim 2:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosefta_Shekalim_2.14"},"witness":"Tosefta Shekalim"},{"reference":"Mishnah Shekalim 5:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Shekalim_5.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-05","he":[369,437],"en":[725,746],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_18b.4"},"reference":"Chagigah 18b:4","assessment":"Chagigah names him and says he ate at the purity standard of sacred food all his life. The implicit ordinary-food interpretation is Heilprin’s explicit wording.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chagigah 18b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_18b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Mishnah Chagigah 2:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Chagigah_2.7"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-06","he":[461,512],"en":[849,860],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_10a.20"},"reference":"Horayot 10a:20","assessment":"Horayot names the two students and their capacity to estimate the number of drops in the sea. The celestial calculation in the preceding passage is Rabbi Yehoshua’s.","evidence":[{"reference":"Horayot 10a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_10a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Horayot 10a:19","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_10a.19"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-07","he":[500,518],"en":[902,915],"target":{"entry":517,"paragraph":4},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 517:4","assessment":"The exact reciprocal entry calls him Elazar Chisma’s colleague.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 517:4","target":{"entry":517,"paragraph":4},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-08","he":[519,557],"en":[973,986],"target":{"entry":1757,"paragraph":4},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1757:4","assessment":"The internal pointer leads to the exact gate-shutting incident. Arakhin preserves the difference in their roles.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1757:4","target":{"entry":1757,"paragraph":4},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Arakhin 11b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Arakhin_11b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-09","he":[598,620],"en":[1060,1094],"target":{"entry":1814,"paragraph":3},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1814:3","assessment":"The ben Nuri notice juxtaposes the Sifrei name and the Horayot name. Yuchasin explicitly prefers the latter reading.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1814:3","target":{"entry":1814,"paragraph":3},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-10","he":[622,666],"en":[1166,1177],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_55b.13"},"reference":"Chullin 55b:13","assessment":"The baraita names Elazar Safra and Yochanan ben Gudgeda as joint witnesses and spells out their ruling of disqualification.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 55b:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_55b.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-11","he":[668,774],"en":[1193,1210],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_7.9"},"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 7:9","assessment":"Eduyot names Nechunya. Gittin gives essentially the same four testimonies under Yochanan, and Yevamot shares the first testimony under Yochanan.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 7:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_7.9"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Gittin 5:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Gittin_5.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Yevamot 14:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Yevamot_14.2"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-12","he":[668,774],"en":[1245,1255],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Gittin_5.5"},"reference":"Mishnah Gittin 5:5","assessment":"Eduyot names Nechunya. Gittin gives essentially the same four testimonies under Yochanan, and Yevamot shares the first testimony under Yochanan.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Gittin 5:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Gittin_5.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 7:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_7.9"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Yevamot 14:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Yevamot_14.2"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-13","he":[439,459],"en":[1260,1272],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Yevamot_14.2"},"reference":"Mishnah Yevamot 14:2","assessment":"The chapter begins with ben Nuri and the next mishnah gives ben Gudgeda’s divorce testimony. That testimony does not directly attest his lifelong purity practice.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Yevamot 14:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Yevamot_14.2"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Yevamot 14:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Yevamot_14.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-14","he":[819,838],"en":[1445,1458],"target":{"entry":1631,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1631:1","assessment":"The internal Yehudah ben Gudgeda entry points back, and Yuchasin recognizes a shared patronymic. The asserted family relation remains attributed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1631:1","target":{"entry":1631,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-15","he":[840,859],"en":[1460,1479],"target":{"entry":2482,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 2482:1","assessment":"The internal Menachem entry directly repeats the contemporaneity claim. The consecutive Mishnah testimonies support the location, while the dating remains the compiler’s inference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2482:1","target":{"entry":2482,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 7:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_7.8"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 7:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_7.9"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-16","he":[861,993],"en":[1695,1706],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_3a.4"},"reference":"Chagigah 3a:4","assessment":"The Bavli preserves the competing grandson and nephew readings. It reports their attendance and recovered speech.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chagigah 3a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_3a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chagigah 3a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_3a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-17","he":[994,1094],"en":[1715,1744],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Terumot_1.1.10"},"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Terumot 1:1:10","assessment":"The Yerushalmi independently reports his sons and the care of purity-sensitive foods. Keep the direct-son tradition distinct from the Bavli alternatives.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Terumot 1:1:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Terumot_1.1.10"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]},{"id":"1818:1:link-18","he":[1096,1110],"en":[1903,1926],"target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/גלגולי_נשמות_אות_א"},"reference":"Gilgulei Neshamot, Alef §9","assessment":"Gilgulei Neshamot, Alef §9, gives the named Eldad and Medad identification, genealogy, divorce and both explanations of the speech impairment. This is the cited author’s mystical explanation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Gilgulei Neshamot, Alef §9","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/גלגולי_נשמות_אות_א"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,12,5,7,8,9,10,13,14,15,16,17],"holds":[{"raw":"הלוי ושוער במקדש","reason":"Arakhin gives the gate assignment. The explicitly Levite heading is corroborated as a report in Yuchasin, whose priestly-guard explanation is an interpretation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Arakhin 11b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Arakhin_11b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ובמשנה יבמות ר\"פ חרש","reason":"Yevamot 14:1–2 includes the named sages and a divorce ruling. A direct reference there for the lifetime purity practice has not been identified.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Yevamot 14:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Yevamot_14.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Yevamot 14:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Yevamot_14.2"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"raw":"לכן לא הביאו הרמב\"ם (יוחסין אצל ר' נחוניא)","reason":"Maimonides refers readers from Eduyot to Gittin for the testimonies. The exact Yuchasin passage assigning the reason for omitting Nechunya from the list remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rambam on Mishnah Eduyot 7:9:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rambam_on_Mishnah_Eduyot_7.9.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"raw":"אחיו ר' יהודה","reason":"The reciprocal entry and Yuchasin support the shared patronymic. A directly stated primary witness for the brother relation remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1631:1","target":{"entry":1631,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"}]},{"raw":"מנחם בן סגנאי בזמנו","reason":"The two Mishnah rulings are adjacent and Heilprin’s other entry repeats the dating. Independent evidence of the exact contemporaneity remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2482:1","target":{"entry":2482,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 7:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_7.8"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 7:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_7.9"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"raw":"בני בתו או בני אחותו","reason":"The two Bavli kinship readings both stand. The Yerushalmi and Tosefta’s report about his sons is a separate tradition.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chagigah 3a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_3a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chagigah 3a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_3a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The exact Yuchasin lemma preserves the priestly guard inference and the differing appointment names. Sukkah supplies the reason for the additional share. Preserve the distinct Temple rosters, testimony name variants and kinship reports. The exact Alef account verifies the attribution of the mystical explanation.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Horayot 10a:19","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_10a.19"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Horayot 10a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_10a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Horayot 10a:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_10a.21"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 55b:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_55b.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chagigah 3a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_3a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chagigah 3a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_3a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Terumot 1:1:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Terumot_1.1.10"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Arakhin 11b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Arakhin_11b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium, Yochanan ben Gudgeda","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource digital Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Sukkah 56a:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_56a.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sukkah 56b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_56b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sukkah 56b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_56b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Mishnah Tamid 1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Tamid_1.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Middot 1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Middot_1.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Tosefta Shekalim (Lieberman) 2:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.